    "question": "Beth had 150 students in her 10th-grade class.  The following year 30 more students join.  In her final year, 15 students left.  How many students did Beth have in her class at the end of her final year?",
    "gold": "165",
    "answer": "Beth had 150 students her 10th-grade year, and added 30 more the following for a total of 150+30= <<150+30=180>>180 students\nIn her final year, 15 students left her class, bringing her total to 180-15=165 students\n#### 165"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the number of students Beth had in her class at the end of her final year, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Start with the initial number of students in Beth's class.\n2. Add the number of students who joined the following year.\n3. Subtract the number of students who left in the final year.\n\nLet's go through the calculations step by step:\n\n1. Initial number of students: 150\n2. Number of students who joined the following year: 30\n   \\[\n   150 + 30 = 180\n   \\]\n   So, after the following year, Beth had 180 students.\n3. Number of students who left in the final year: 15\n   \\[\n   180 - 15 = 165\n   \\]\n   So, at the end of her final year, Beth had 165 students.\n\nTherefore, the number of students Beth had in her class at the end of her final year is \\boxed{165}.",
